#Smart Contract Overview

Smart contract is self-executing program or code that runs on a blockchain.
Ethereum Virtual Machine (EVM) is a crucial component of the Ethereum blockchain that allows the execution of smart contracts.
when deploying a contract 
   1. complie solidity to bytecode.
   2. send transaction containing the bytcode to EVM node.
   3. the node calculates the address of new contract.
Solidity is a high-level language 
Opcode is a low-level instruction that tells the EVM what to operation to prform.
Gas is static to Opcode that is running for ADD and MUL Gas amount is fixed for complex Opcode like SSTORE it is calculated.
Gas is dependent on the Opcode
Contracts are compiled to create bytcode.
The data field contain created bycode.
The to field is left blank to deploy a contract.
Contract will have address, balance and runtime bytecode.
Transaction begins at an EOA.
EOA- (externally owned account)
Transaction occurs sequentially.
Transaction set a gas limit.
Transaction send calldata targetting contract.
Smart contracts can call each other within the one transaction.

Solidity value type
    1. unsigned integer- number without sign(not positive or negative).
    2. integer- number either positive or negative.
    3. boolean- either true or false.
    4. Enum - defining option for value by name.
